      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi,\n\nSorry, i think there is a confusion here.\n\"charger_dump\" command is an existing command implemented in charger/driver/ files \n\nex: DECLARE_CONSOLE_COMMAND(charger_dump, console_bd9995x_dump_regs,\n\t\t\tNULL,\n\t\t\t\"Dump all charger registers\");\n\nwe can find similar implementation in files\nex:\ndriver/charger/bq25710.c\ndriver/charger/bd9995x.c\ndriver/charger/isl923x.c\ndriver/charger/isl9241.c and driver/charger/sm5803.c\n\nI have placed this code from driver files to common/charger.c file. Hence from change set it looks like i might have added a new command but its an existing command.\n\nYes we can club both the commands \"charger\" and \"charger_dump\".\nbut I feel keeping it as a separate command will increase the readability and easy usage.\n\nI found we have separate dump commands implemented similar to this in EC i.e \n\"tcpci_dump\" \"ppc_dump\" \"pe \u003cport\u003e dump\" commands.",
